## Summary
The article discusses an investigation into a painting attributed to Valentin de Boulogne, which if authentic, could be worth 5.5 million euros. It involves art critic Sgarbi and suggests that the case may not lead to any significant outcome.

## Key Points
- The case centers on a presumed painting by Valentin de Boulogne, a French Caravaggist artist.
- If authenticated, the painting is estimated to have a value of 5.5 million euros.
- Sgarbi has commented that the investigation is unlikely to result in a meaningful conclusion.
- The authenticity of the painting is under scrutiny in the ongoing inquiry.


